WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.060
Film Courage: Looking at your IMDB [page]
you have 31 or so producing credits.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.290
I’m sure there are going to be more by the
time of this video releases.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.770
Which production taught you the most?

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:09.870
Passionflix co-founder Tosca Musk: Wow!

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:15.070
Well, I learned a lot on so many of the different
movies that I’ve done, so it depends on

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.910
what did I learn?

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:26.199
I’ve made a lot of movies and I think that
the ones that have taught me the most are

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:29.609
I made a movie called HAVENHURST (that one
taught me a lot).

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:31.230
It was a horror to me, it was horror film.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:35.420
It was very difficult and I realize there
are many things that I will not do again,

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.990
so that’s a great thing to learn.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:44.641
Great movie, the movie ultimately ended up
being very good, but the experience for me

00:00:44.641 --> 00:00:49.390
as a producer was not a great one.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:56.390
The things that I’ve learned the most, I
mean I’ve made a lot of movies.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:03.150
I think ultimately the best lesson that I’ve
learned which is from making the Passionflix

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:08.870
movies is that I need to enjoy the experience
from start to finish because it is very hard

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.110
to make a movie and it costs a lot of money.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.360
And if you’re not enjoying it, then there
is no reason to do it.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:21.570
So I learned that from making these movies
prior to this (prior to Passionflix) realizing

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:29.640
that (from hindsight) I did not enjoy making
a lot of those movies and I do enjoy making

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.640
the Passionflix movies.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.200
They’re fulfilling, they make me happy,
I can’t wait to make the next one.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:41.590
Whereas prior to that I was not enjoying them,
it was more of a job.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:45.390
Not to say they were bad experiences, I made
some great movies and I really enjoyed the

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:50.350
people and fortunately now with Passionflix
I get to bring so many of those people on

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.340
to my productions.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:58.530
But sometimes when you are working for other
people and you’re getting notes from them,

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:06.190
they’re not necessarily the notes that I
would probably…how can I say this?

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:09.869
Sometimes their interpretation of what the
movie should be is not my interpretation of

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:11.970
what the movie should be and that is filmmaking.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.230
I mean that’s the creative process.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:19.770
I don’t necessarily want to show women in
a certain light and so I didn’t enjoy that

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.780
specific film.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.970
And now I get to show a woman in the light
that I like to show them, so it makes me happy.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.190
I just like to have positive experiences in
film, I think that’s the important thing.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:33.280
The Tiki Bar TV which was a podcast that I
did (a video podcast that I did) was a perfect

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.260
example of making something and really enjoying
it every single time you made it because it

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:44.680
was funny and the people were great and so
now I get to do that again.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.599
Please do come to one of our sets when we
make the next one.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:51.130
We are laughing and joking and having the
best time.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:56.710
The crew that I have on all of my movies are
almost the same crew for the last year.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:03:03.209
They just come, they transplant back, they
all come to my new sets because we have great

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:05.470
experiences and it’s just so much fun.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.040
Film Courage: Environment is so important.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.360
Tosca Musk: Environment is vital.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:16.000
Especially it’s high-pressure, it’s time-sensitive,
and you have to be creative within these confines.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.510
And we don’t have the luxury (yet) of being
able to say “Oh, we’ll just do it tomorrow.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:25.410
We’ll just pick it up and let’s just lengthen
the time frame of this movie.”

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:29.989
We need to shoot these movies in 15, 16 days
and we need to get them out and we have fans

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:35.810
that we release the movie on one day, the
next day they say “Where’s the next movie?”

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.319
It takes 5 months to make a movie at minimum!

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:41.459
And so we are trying very hard to get them
out as quickly as possible.

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:47.879
So we need to make the experience fun and
we need to make sure that we are all in this

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:54.390
positive, creative environment so that we
can create the best movie.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:04:02.569
Film Courage: Sure and too if you are doing
sensitive scenes with the actors to have it

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:03.980
where you feel safe [on set].

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.500
That’s what I was saying [earlier], I felt
that when I watched the [Passionflix] behind

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.480
the scenes footage, just kind of a feeling
of being safe.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.480
Tosca Musk: Thank you!

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:15.180
Yeah, it’s very important that the actors
are comfortable on our set and my crew is

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:22.030
extremely respectful and every single time
we come to any of these scenes, I have a conversation

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.490
with my actors, I need to make sure that they
are comfortable.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:29.560
We will rehearse everything, we will then
move forward with more.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:35.689
The sets are closed and we’re constantly
talking about where a hand should be, what

00:04:35.689 --> 00:04:36.689
it should be.

00:04:36.689 --> 00:04:41.650
This is not just willy-nilly “Go ahead and
try things!”

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:47.150
We’re very specific on where the camera
is, what we’ll do, where we are following

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:50.029
hands and what I want those hands to do.

00:04:50.029 --> 00:04:59.120
And I have to make sure that both my male
and female actors feel comfortable with what

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.020
I need to portray.

